# panes.conf — the iTerm panes the companion's boot-app opens at login.
# COPY to panes.conf (gitignored) and list YOUR services.
#
# One pane per line:  <Name>|<command to run in that pane>
# Order top→bottom. The generator lays them out as alternating splits and
# adds the SSH-launch window guard automatically.
#
# The doctrine: every long-running service gets a VISIBLE pane that at least
# tails its log. "If I can't see it working, I can't trust it's working."
# One-shot bulk jobs do NOT get a pane — they run detached + report via a
# status command (see the wiki concept page).
#
# Example (commented placeholders):
# Repo Puller|cd /Users/youruser/work/companion-mac && bash lib/repo-puller.sh
# Example Worker|cd /Users/youruser/work/companion-mac/services/example && ./worker.sh
